meta {
  name: Turn
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/apis/{{site}}/api/copilot/turn
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "patient_uuid": "{{patientUuid}}",
    "question": "What is the recommended BP target for this patient, and is anything urgent?",
    "ask_evidence": true
  }
}

docs {
  # Turn

  UC2/UC7 — `POST /api/copilot/turn`, the follow-up Q&A turn. Requires the
  `user/turn.write` scope and the `patients`/`med` ACL. Runs the
  deterministic critical subset unconditionally (panic labs, drug-drug,
  drug-allergy, open follow-ups — R13; these ship even on a degraded turn)
  and attempts a verified, chart-grounded answer; an invented citation is
  moved to `answer.rejected` rather than shipped as provenance (R6/R10).

  ## ask_evidence toggle

  The example body above sets `"ask_evidence": true` — the physician's
  explicit UC7 request for reranked, cited guideline evidence this turn
  (real MariaDB hybrid FULLTEXT+VECTOR retrieval + Cohere embed/rerank,
  never an inferred NLP classification of the question). To exercise the
  plain Week 1 flow instead, drop the `ask_evidence` key (or set it
  `false`) — the response shape is identical either way, just without
  guideline-sourced grounded claims.

  ## prior_turns (optional)

  Add an optional `"prior_turns": ["What changed since the last visit?"]`
  array to carry earlier question text into this turn's context.

  Every citation `token` in the response is resolvable via the Source
  Resolve request in this collection — that's the click-to-source loop.
}
